// test_gui_notify_registration.hv — guards the extraction of gui.notify out of
// the core-facing UIBridge translation unit.
//
// What: calls gui.notify and asserts the call resolves to a real host
//       function instead of an unresolved identifier.
// Why:  gui.notify was moved from src/host/module/bridges/UIBridge.cpp into
//       src/host/module/bridges/qt/QtGuiBridge.cpp (havel_gui target only),
//       and its registration now goes through the weak hook
//       installQtGuiBridge. A weak symbol that fails to resolve, or a
//       registration lost in the move, shows up here as
//       "Unresolved identifier 'notify'" at compile time — this test fails.
// Expected: assert passes. The returned value is false because the smoke
//       harness has no QApplication/GUIManager; the point is that the host
//       function is registered, not that a notification appears.

// Referencing gui.notify must compile. If the Qt bridge did not register it,
// the pipeline raises a SemanticError before the assertion is ever reached.
res = gui.notify("smoke", "gui.notify is registered by the Qt bridge")

assert(res == false, "gui.notify must be registered and return false without a GUI")
